From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:53:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] squash! ports/arkweb: Servo as an alternative ArkWeb webview
 backend

Move the port from OpenHarmony-7.0-Beta1 to OpenHarmony-v7.0-Release.

The NWeb headers are re-synced from web_webview 12cb9a37bbba. The release
inserts new virtuals in the middle of NWeb (GetSurfaceNodeId,
GetSurfaceRSHandle, ...) and removes OnTouchCancelById, so a shim built
against the Beta1 headers no longer matches the vtable of the 7.0
libraries. The stub bases are regenerated from the new headers.

The new ohos-patches/0002 fixes base/startup/init, which tests the
undefined macro __LP__ instead of __LP64__ and therefore looks up seccomp
filters under lib/seccomp on 64-bit builds: appspawn fails to install its
filter and exits, and init reboots the device in a loop. Every 64-bit
7.0-Release image needs it, with or without Servo. The rebase of 0001 is
a separate squash! for the RTLD_LOCAL patch, which edits that file later
in the stack.

Validation: Built a full rk3568 arm64 image from OpenHarmony-v7.0-Release with ohos-patches/0001 and 0002 applied (without 0002 it boot-loops on appspawn) and flashed a HiHope DAYU200 (OpenHarmony 7.0, API 26); `./mach build --ohos --release --no-package -p arkweb`, deployed with `tools/deploy.py`, test app installed with `tools/build_test_app.py`; `HDC_TARGET=<serial> uv run --with pytest --with hdc-py --with pillow python -m pytest ports/arkweb/tools`: 35 passed, 1 xfailed. `tools/gen_stubs.py --check` is clean.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; header sync, OpenHarmony image build and boot-loop fix, on-device testing)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
